WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.705
This module's subject is
the collector itself,

2
00:00:02.705 --> 00:00:06.688
so its requirements are the ones the
collector's identity has to meet.

3
00:00:06.688 --> 00:00:11.681
Least privilege, A C six in NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three:

4
00:00:11.681 --> 00:00:15.138
each script holds only the
permissions its calls need.

5
00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:18.696
Authenticator management, I
A five: no long-lived secret,

6
00:00:18.696 --> 00:00:24.112
and ScubaGear's application-credential
policies apply to the program's own apps too.

7
00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:26.224
Continuous monitoring, C A seven,

8
00:00:26.224 --> 00:00:29.663
depends on collectors that
return complete results.

9
00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:33.892
And BOD 25-01 requires
the SCuBA assessment tools

10
00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:37.063
and continuous reporting
for in-scope tenants.

11
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:39.937
Book 02's Appendix A has the mapping.

12
00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:44.732
The evidence an ISSO keeps: for each
collector, its cloud, endpoint,

13
00:00:44.732 --> 00:00:50.148
app registration, credential type,
exact permissions and consent record,

14
00:00:50.148 --> 00:00:53.860
plus the call list and its
tests in the repository.
